AB  - This study examined the potential of employing LLM for design parameter sensitivity analysis in mechanical component design. Two approaches were investigated: chatbot-based platforms and agent systems integrated with finite element analysis (FEA) tools. Experiments using chatbot platforms produced reference-level responses, underscoring the need for caution in practical applications. In the agent-based experiments, direct reliance on raw FEA outputs did not yield accurate results; however, incorporating information analyzed through analysis of variance (ANOVA) enabled correct sensitivity rankings. These findings demonstrate that integrating LLM with engineering analysis tools can enhance design efficiency. Nevertheless, practical implementation may vary depending on economic considerations and the nature of specific design tasks. Consequently, the development of specialized platforms or integrated tools capable of flexibly addressing diverse design problems is essential. © 2025 The Korean Society of Mechanical Engineers.
