AD  - Artificial Intelligence & Data Science, KJ Somaiya Institute of Technology, Mumbai, India
AB  - FastWrite is a Python-based framework that automates the creation and evaluation of software documentation by harnessing advanced Natural Language Processing and multiple large language model backends. It analyzes source code via Python’s Abstract Syntax Tree to generate inline comments, comprehensive function and module descriptions, Graphviz-compatible data flow diagrams and illustrative code examples, all through a unified command-line or programmatic interface. FastWrite supports both cloud-hosted and on-premise AI models—such as OpenAI’s GPT series, Google Gemini, Groq LLMs and Ollama deployments—allowing developers to tailor performance and privacy tradeoffs. In addition, it incorporates objective quality metrics, including BLEU-based scoring, to assess and benchmark the fidelity of generated documentation against reference standards. Through seamless integration with Python 3.11+ environments, FastWrite addresses the persistent challenge of maintaining up-to-date, high-quality documentation, streamlines developer workflows and promotes reproducibility and best practices in modern software engineering. Keywords: NLP, Code documentation, AST Parsing, Python, BLEU Score. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Dr. Vivek Sunnapwar, Dr. Hariram Chavan and Dr. Namrata F. Ansari; individual chapters, the contributors.
