AB  - The proceedings contain 39 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Towards Autonomous Robotic Systems. The topics include: A New Semi-Automatic Strategy for Teleoperating Mobile Manipulators Using a Haptic Device; mixed Reality Visualisations for Interpretable Transparent Robot Behaviour; leveraging Stable Diffusion for Monocular Depth Estimation via Image Semantic Encoding; marker Density of Optical Tactile Sensor for Moving Object Tracking; Automated USMN Integration for Precision Robotics and Large-Scale Metrology; frequency Map Enhancement Revisited and Extended for Biohybrid Robotics; towards a Modular Compliant Actuator Toolkit; multi-Contact Posture Generation Using Vector Field Inequalities; acrobotics: A Generalist Approach to Quadrupedal Robots’ Parkour; An Integrated LQR and Sliding Mode Controller for Balance and Motion Control of a Five-Link Two-Wheel Legged Robot; analysis of Adaptive Passive Technologies for the Robot Traversal in Unstructured Environments; practical Handling of Dynamic Environments in Decentralised Multi-Robot Patrol; acquiring Tactile Skills on a Quadruped Robot Using Vision-Based Soft Tactile Sensors; multiClear: Multimodal Soft Exoskeleton Glove for Transparent Object Grasping Assistance; towards Accurate Shape Prediction for Compact Spring Backbone Tendon-Driven Continuum Robots; Locomotion of Multi Arm Robot for In-Orbit Operations (MARIO) in Lab Environment; surveying Deliberation Practices and Methodological Needs in Robotics Software Engineering; saFliTe: Fuzzing Autonomous Systems via Large Language Models; Varanus: Runtime Verification for CSP; Preliminary Study of DSL Code Generation for Robotics with LLMs; A Verification Methodology for Safety Assurance of RAS; Towards Digital Twin Aided Autonomy for a UR3e Robotic Manipulator: (Invited Paper); scenario-Based System Testing for Distributed Robotics Applications: (Invited Paper); revisiting Formal Methods for Autonomous Robots: A Structured Survey: (Invite