AB  - The proceedings contain 30 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Agile Software Development. The topics include: Generative AI for Test Driven Development: Preliminary Results; Responsible AI in Agile Software Engineering - An Industry Perspective; A Journey Through SPACE: Unpacking the Perceived Productivity of GitHub Copilot; analyzing the Impact of Constant Feedback on Hybrid Agile Team Performance: Preliminary Results; dual Effects of Hybrid Working on Performance: More Work Hours or More Work Time; hybrid Meetings in Agile Software Development; agile Approaches in Critical Infrastructures; social Capital in Software Product Management: A Case Study From a Large-Scale Agile Context; ChatGPT for Tailoring Software Documentation for Managers and Developers; The AI Scrum Master: Using Large Language Models (LLMs) to Automate Agile Project Management Tasks; copilot’s Island of Joy: Balancing Individual Satisfaction with Team Interaction in Agile Development; Can ChatGPT Suggest Patterns? An Exploratory Study About Answers Given by AI-Assisted Tools to Design Problems; towards Improving Behavior-Driven Development and Acceptance Testing-Driven Development Teaching in a University Project Course; agile Software Engineering Capstone Courses: Exploring the Impact of Gender; towards Continuous Certification of Software Systems for Aerospace; shared Leadership for Better Understanding Agile Teams; design Framework for Software Startups Applying Remote Work; bridging Silos: Amplifying InnerSource Adoption Using an Activity Theory Perspective; where Do Developers Admit their Security-Related Concerns?; digital Twin Adapted Agile Software Development Life Cycle; drawing Based Game for Teaching Scrum; selected Concepts of Leadership in Self-organizing Teams; towards a Double-Edged Sword: Modelling the Impact in Agile Software Development; An Agile Mindset in a VUCA-World; the Right Amount of Technical Debt in an Agile Context; stories Vs. User Stories: A Terminological Clarification.
