AB  - The proceedings contain 47 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Innovative Perspectives on Computational Intelligence and Data Science. The topics include: AugRoSent: Boosting Romanian Sentiment Analysis Through Advanced Data Augmentation; evaluating Large Language Models for Diacritic Restoration in Romanian Texts: A Comparative Study; Human-Robot Interaction: Real-Time Control of Robotic Systems via ROS2 and Unity; intelligent Cyber-Social Ecosystem Industry 5.0; distributed Learning for Next-Gen Recommender Systems: A Survey; comparative Analysis of Edge Computing Architectures for IoT Systems: Towards Scalable, Secure and Sustainable Deployments; comparative Evaluation of Flow-Based Feature Extraction Tools for IoT Cyberattack Detection; Multi-Quantum Agent System for DNA Self-Assembly; Quantum Clustering for Classification of DNA Sequences; free-Range Chicken Farms Oriented Bird Detection; Innovative Medical Image Analyzer - iMIA Tested on COVID-19 Images; technical Debt, Empirical Study, Human Aspects in Software Engineering; Survey on Cybersecurity in Precision Agriculture: Threat Landscape, Defense Strategies, Ethics and EU Regulations; analyzing Similarity Across Investment Portfolios: A Multi-dimensional Approach; association Rule Mining for Combinatorial Biomarker Discovery. A Case Study on Type 2 Diabetes; Exploratory Analysis and Classification of Lymphoma DNA Methylation Data; applying L-Moments Statistical Theory to Analyze Real-World Sensor Data from Orchards; optimizing Diabetes Risk Prediction: Comparative Analysis of Machine Learning Models and Feature Importance; multi-view Sky Image Regression for Enhanced Photovoltaic Power Forecasting; l-Moments for Robust Temporal Data Drift Monitoring in Agricultural IoT Systems; AI-Based Sensor Optimization and Anomaly Detection in Water Distribution Networks; assessment of Groundwater Quality of the Republic of Ireland Using Random Forest Algorithm.
