AB  - This article aims to explore a brand-new software development paradigm based on generative artificial intelligence and evaluate its application potential in the construction of digital library management systems. The research focuses on an innovative technical route: using the Google Stitch platform for the automated design and code generation of the front-end UI/UX, and leveraging the TRAE integrated AI development environment to lead the back-end database design, test data generation, and business logic development based on the Python/Django framework. This paper first constructs the system architecture of this intelligent development mode, and then deeply analyzes its revolutionary advantages in improving development efficiency, lowering technical thresholds, and accelerating iterative verification. Meanwhile, the article also conducts a prudent and critical analysis of its inherent potential risks. The research conclusion holds that this AI-driven development model has brought about a disruptive transformation to software engineering. However, when applied to core business systems, a "human-machine collaboration" hybrid strategy should be adopted, leveraging AI to accelerate prototype design and automate routine tasks while retaining strict manual review, quality control, and architectural dominance, in order to balance innovation efficiency and long-term system stability. Copyright © (2026) by Aussino Academic Publishing House All rights reserved.
