AB  - This paper addresses the substantial workload associated with traditional digital signal processor (DSP) motor control software development by proposing a method to automatically generate C code from system models using the Simulink modeling platform, thereby significantly reducing the motor control development cycle. The working principles and development framework of the automatic code generation technology based on Model-Based Design (MBD) are first elucidated. Subsequently, a Space Vector Pulse Width Modulation (SVPWM) algorithm simulation model is established within Simulink. Finally, the generated code is deployed onto a DSP control system hardware platform for experimental validation. The results demonstrate that the application of MBD enables rapid DSP code generation, improves motor development efficiency, and achieves the desired control performance.  © 2025 IEEE.
