AD  - Xi'an Jiaotong University, School of Mechanical Engineering, Xi'an, China
AB  - Nuclear power engineering, as a high-risk and high-technology-intensive industry, relies heavily on refined management and information support in its construction and operation. With the advancement of global nuclear power digital transformation, conventional digital management practices often suffer from information silos and low efficiency in knowledge transfer, particularly in platform administration, project execution, and the application of 3D design software. This paper proposes a nuclear power engineering digital management assistance system based on Large Language Models (LLMs) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), which integrates planning documents, management documents, and technical documents to achieve intelligent support for functional management, platform management, project management, and 3D software development. The system's primary methods include: standardized preprocessing and semantic segmentation of historical digital documents; structured parsing of knowledge files; establishment of a vectorized knowledge base with a re-ranking retrieval mechanism; and a RAG-enhanced intelligent Q&A module for generating management recommendations. Using digital management documents for nuclear power plant engineering design from 2023 to 2025 as the dataset, we have conducted comprehensive experiments to evaluate the system's performance. Our findings validate the effectiveness of integrating RAG technology with LLMs for digital management tasks and provide valuable insights for the future development of intelligent engineering design assistance systems. © 2025 IEEE.
