AB  - Computer technology advancements have revolutionized recommender systems through sophisticated algorithmic optimization and neural network architectures. This technical survey examines computational methods and software engineering solutions for generative recommendation systems, emphasizing deep learning implementation strategies, data structure optimization, and algorithm performance enhancement. Our research focuses on core computer science technologies: advanced neural network architectures including Variational Autoencoders (VAEs), Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs), diffusion algorithms, and transformer-based computational models. We present systematic algorithmic categorization of four computational paradigms: interaction-pattern algorithms, content-generation algorithms, conversational computing systems, and multimodal data processing techniques. Through technical analysis of over 150 computational implementations, we evaluate algorithmic performance metrics, computational complexity optimization, and software architecture improvements. Key technological contributions include: (1) algorithm efficiency enhancement through optimized data structures, (2) neural network architecture refinement for improved computational performance, (3) distributed computing frameworks for scalable recommendation processing, and (4) memory management optimization techniques. This technical resource provides comprehensive algorithmic solutions and software engineering methodologies for computer scientists developing next-generation recommendation computing systems.  © 2025 IEEE.
