AB  - The identification of errors in code via automated code analysis and repair is of ever-growing importance in modern software development and education. This paper describes a language agnostic code debugging assistant that will detect syntax and logical errors across many programming languages and return suggestions in real time. The freeform model operates by applying a generative large language model (LLM) on the user's input code, running the LLM for explanations as well as modified snippets. The assistant was developed using a basic web framework to provide an overall senior (but not entirely senior) user experience, while offering users maximum flexibility in terms of language and code input. In summary, the proposed system is an entry to the debugging process, to support code quality reliability, and to assist both developers and learners in improving productivity and accuracy in their programming.  © 2025 IEEE.
