AB  - We developed an advanced human-robot collaborative design method for the development of complex software systems. The method addresses the challenges posed by intricate architectures and heterogeneous integration by introducing efficient software synthesis paradigms and leveraging generative artificial intelligence (AI). Based on closed-loop, multimodal embodied planning principles, the method enhances system modeling capabilities and supports rigorous functionality verification. To assess its effectiveness, the method was applied to four customized software development projects. Detailed records were maintained for each project, including development time, algorithmic complexity, testing duration, and debugging effort. These metrics enabled a comparative performance analysis against traditional development approaches. The results demonstrated that the method with large language model (LLM) technologies presented substantial improvements across all evaluation metrics of software development, including efficiency, accuracy, and adaptability. © 2025 IEEE.
