AB  - As sustainability becomes a priority for organizations, the integration of green software engineering into business project management reduces environmental impact while maintaining technological innovation. Green software engineering focuses on designing, developing, and deploying software solutions with minimal energy consumption and resource use, aligning technical decisions with environmental goals. When integrated with project management frameworks, this approach encourages sustainable practices across the software lifecycle. For businesses, adopting green software principles supports corporate social responsibility while driving long-term efficiency, compliance with environmental regulations, and a competitive edge in eco-conscious markets. This intersection of sustainability and project management represents a shift in how digital solutions are built and managed. Green Software Engineering for Business Project Management explores the convergence of governance, sustainability, software engineering, and business project management. It examines strategic insights, applied frameworks, and empirical studies from academia and industry. This book covers topics such as data analytics, circular economy, and sustainable development, and is a useful resource for computer engineers, business owners, academicians, researchers, and scientists. Coverage: The many academic areas covered in this publication include, but are not limited to: Artificial Intelligence Business Project Management Circular Economy Cloud Computing Data Analytics Environmental Science Ethics and Law Geospatial Technology Green Engineering Healthcare Systems Large Language Models Soft Robotics Software Engineering Software Lifecycle Management Supply Chains and Logistics Sustainable Development. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
