AB  - Existing techniques often depend on manual processes or limited models for machine learning that do not capture complex, multimodal dependencies between code, infrastructure and runtime behaviour. This paper presents an AI-driven approach using Large Language Models (LLMs) for efficient bug triaging and proactive root cause analysis. Our system integrates graph-based modelling, multimodal learning, and LLMs to automatically triage bugs, predict root causes, and generate effective test cases for bug reproduction. We evaluate the proposed framework's effectiveness using various basic models from existing literature, including traditional machine-learning classifiers and graph-based models. The results show that our method is significantly higher than the baseline approaches in the average time to resolution (MTTR), the accuracy of the root cause (RCA) and the effectiveness of the test case (THE), achieving a reduction of MTTR by more than 50%, an RCA of 84.7% and a THE of 83.2%. Our approach improves the efficiency and accuracy of bug triaging and software quality assurance by generating reliable test cases.  © 2025 IEEE.
