AB  - Project management is evolving in the era of smart automation through artificial intelligence, which has streamlined the delegation process, tracking, and managing tasks. The AI technology streamlines efficiency through automated assignment of tasks to employees according to their competencies, balancing their workload, and, through predictive analytics, anticipating the challenges beforehand. These innovations are not only helping make decisions and manage risks but also making seamless collaboration possible, eliminating drudgery, and increasing rates of project completion. AI-based systems provide timely information, automatic reminders, and personalized recommendations, which allow for better execution and superior output. Despite issues of ethical considerations and integration, AI makes the Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC) considerably easier through cost reduction and minimized human errors. Involvement of AI in project management has unprecedented capacity to enhance optimization of resources, better communication, and ongoing learning, framing the future agenda of resource-aware and adaptable project deployment. © 2025 IEEE.
