AB  - Business process modeling is a key technique in enterprise management. It assumes graphical description of activities, events and decisions that occur in organizational and information systems. Therefore, business process models should be of high-quality to ensure efficient workflow design, analysis, and improvement. However, the growth in popularity of AI-assistants based on large language models, opens the possibility for business process model generation using text descriptions. Nevertheless, the quality and usability of such models requires further study. Therefore, this paper presents the software tool for evaluation of AI-generated Business Process Model and Notation (BPMN) models from the structural perspective using related measures, as well as the comparison with the human-designed models. © 2025 IEEE.
