AB  - This paper presents a systematic three-phase framework for legacy database and web application modernization using Large Language Models as intelligent automation agents. The framework encompasses investigation, planning, and execution phases where AI agents perform source code archaeology, documentation generation, and strategic migration planning. Empirical validation demonstrates substantial efficiency improvements, with modernization efforts reduced from multi-day manual processes to hours and database modernization achieving 95% time reduction. The framework addresses critical gaps in existing methodologies by enabling systematic infrastructure transformation while preserving institutional knowledge. © 2025 IEEE.
