AB  - Due to rapidly changing requirements and the need for reduced development time, the difficulty of software development for the industrial cyber-physical system is continuously increasing. A new top-down system design method is needed to improve efficiency and ensure correctness. This paper proposes a contract-based specification search and completion method for automatic code generation of industrial edge applications. Contracts are introduced for modeling the interface between components in a manufacturing process and automatically selecting candidate components from a predefined library. The feasibility of the proposed method is demonstrated by a case study of an emulated car welding line. The final result shows the development efficiency and software reusability can be significantly improved.  © 2024 IEEE.
