AB  - Code editing is essential in evolving software development. In literature, several automated code editing tools are proposed, which leverage Information Retrieval-based techniques and Machine Learningbased code generation and code editing models. A patch that is obtained by search & retrieval, even if incorrect, can provide helpful guidance to a code generation model. However, a retrieval-guided patch produced by a code generation model can still be a few tokens off from the intended patch. Such generated patches can be slightly modified to create the intended patches. We propose SarGaM which mimics a developer's behavior - search for related patches, generate or write code and then modify to adapt it to the right context. Our evaluation of SarGaM on edit generation shows superior performance w.r.t. the current state-of-the-art techniques. SarGaM also shows its effectiveness on automated program repair tasks. © 2024 IEEE Computer Society. All rights reserved.
