AB  - The proceedings contain 15 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Fundamental Approaches to Software Engineering. The topics include: Towards Large Language Model Guided Kernel Direct Fuzzing; DeepCRCEval: Revisiting the Evaluation of Code Review Comment Generation; formal Architectural Patterns for Adaptive Robotic Software; compositional Learning for Synchronous Parallel Automata; roboScene: Notation for Formal Verification of Human-Robot Interaction; hybridize Functions: A Tool for Automatically Refactoring Imperative Deep Learning Programs to Graph Execution; VOCE: A Virtual On-Call Engineer for Automated Alert Incident Analysis Using a Large Language Model; symbolic State Partitioning for Reinforcement Learning; fizzer with Local Space Fuzzing: (Competition Contribution); Reasoning about Substitutability at the Level of JVM Bytecode; prove your Colorings: Formal Verification of Cache Coloring of Bao Hypervisor; ESBMC v7.7: Automating Branch Coverage Analysis Using CFG-Based Instrumentation and SMT Solving: (Competition Contribution); preface; ETAPS Foreword.
